Third-party components retained in this tree:

* calib/skunk.s — by tursilion (harmlesslion.com). Its own header grants free
  use for any purpose, commercial or otherwise; that header is kept intact.

* sim/crates/jrom/src/univ.bin — the community "universal header" signed boot
  block (SubQMod), 8192 bytes, embedded so produced .j64 images pass cartridge
  authentication. It is redistributed throughout the Jaguar homebrew ecosystem
  but carries no formal licence of its own. It is NOT covered by the MIT grant
  above. If that matters for your use, build .rom (Alpine) images instead, or
  supply your own header — nothing else in the suite depends on it.
